From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Fri, 24 Jul 2026 06:44:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 07799/11362] [outer-loop] ARC loop iter13: fix goal-absent
 false-positive-win via is_confident_nav goal-present guard
 (REQ-ARC-WMTE-5883)

The E4 latent issue tracked since iter6: is_level_complete/goal_energy read an
ABSENT goal colour as already-won, so a nav game whose plan-start grid lacks the
goal colour makes plan_in_model return a bogus ~1-step 'win' the live E3 agent
executes for zero progress. Fix: is_confident_nav gains an optional grid= param
requiring the goal present at plan-start; scored _induce_and_plan passes
grid=self.root_grid. Fully unit-tested in the model (TestGoalPresentGuard).
tu93 unaffected (goal 14 present in root -> guard is a no-op): 3/3 solve + L3
calibration both CLEAN. 34 nav+hazard tests pass; ruff+mypy clean.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JntPrUGLNesPcJH1pyfFYw
